【設問】
Which of the following statements is true?', NULL, '["Mino’s traditional papermaking techniques were recognized by UNESCO in 2014.","The number of washi workshops in Mino has increased since 1988.","Imai’s colored paper was used only for writing letters.","Sato began his training after the UNESCO designation."]', 0, '["第1段落：2014年にユネスコ無形文化遺産に登録されたと明記。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題）', 903);
INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('tgweb_english', '長文問題', 'リヴァロのチーズ作り', 'Livarot, a small town in the Normandy region of France, has been producing cheese since at least the 17th century. The surrounding pastures, kept green by frequent rainfall, provided ideal grazing conditions for dairy cattle, and the region’s cool, humid climate proved well suited to aging cheese slowly. These conditions allowed Livarot to develop a strong, distinctively flavored cheese that eventually earned legal protection under French regional naming laws in 1975.

Camille Laurent operates one of the few remaining farmhouse dairies producing Livarot cheese by hand. She still washes each wheel of cheese with a saltwater solution during aging, a step that develops its characteristic orange-red rind and sharp aroma. Laurent’s grandmother taught her the process, which she began learning in 1990. At that time, around 20 small producers made Livarot cheese using traditional methods. Today, only five remain, as many farms have shifted to large-scale industrial production.

Laurent frequently mentions Étienne Moreau, a cheesemaker who ran a dairy in Livarot beginning in 1848. Before his time, cheese wheels were often uneven in size and inconsistent in flavor from batch to batch. Moreau introduced standardized molds and more precise aging schedules, which made the cheese’s quality far more consistent. His methods were widely adopted by other producers in the region and are considered the foundation of modern Livarot cheesemaking.

A faded photograph of Moreau’s original dairy hangs in Laurent’s cellar. Like Moreau, she believes that consistency should never come at the expense of traditional flavor. Laurent has trained several younger cheesemakers over the years, and in 2020, one of her former trainees helped organize a regional cheese festival that featured her products alongside those of other small producers. The event significantly increased demand for her cheese. Laurent now hopes to open her dairy for guided tours, allowing visitors to see the aging process and better understand the work behind traditional Livarot cheese.

【設問】
What made the region around Livarot suitable for cheesemaking?', NULL, '["Its dry summers allowed cheese to age quickly.","Its pastures and climate suited dairy farming and slow aging.","Its location near the coast provided salt for free.","Its soil was ideal for growing grain to feed cattle."]', 1, '["第1段落：牧草地と気候が酪農とチーズの熟成に適していた。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題）', 904);
