Which of the following statements is true?', NULL, '["Margaret Ashworth established her workshop in 1832.","The number of clockmaking workshops in Prescot has grown since 1982.","Yardley’s workshop primarily repairs modern digital watches.","Ashworth’s tools were rejected by other workshops in Prescot."]', 0, '["第3段落：Ashworthは1832年に工房を設立と明記。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題）', 905);
INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('tgweb_english', '長文問題', 'アヴェイロのタイル絵付け', 'Aveiro, a coastal city in central Portugal, became known for producing decorative ceramic tiles, called azulejos, beginning in the 16th century. The region’s clay-rich soil provided high-quality raw material, and the city’s canals allowed finished tiles to be transported easily to buildings throughout Portugal. Over time, azulejos became a defining feature of Portuguese architecture, used to decorate churches, train stations, and private homes.

Beatriz Nunes runs a small tile workshop near Aveiro’s historic canal district. She paints each tile by hand using mineral-based pigments mixed according to a formula her grandfather recorded decades ago. Nunes began working in the family workshop in 1995, when the area around Aveiro had about 25 workshops producing hand-painted tiles. Today, only six such workshops remain, as many buyers now purchase mass-produced, machine-printed tiles instead.

Nunes often mentions Manuel Cardoso, a tile painter active in Aveiro beginning in 1867. At the time, most azulejos featured only blue and white patterns copied from earlier styles. Cardoso introduced a wider range of colors and began designing original patterns based on local plants and sea life, rather than repeating traditional geometric designs. His work broadened the artistic possibilities of azulejo painting and influenced tile workshops throughout the region.

A set of Cardoso’s original design sketches is displayed on the wall of Nunes’s workshop. Like Cardoso, she believes that tiles should reflect the character of the place where they are made. Nunes has trained several apprentices, and in 2021, one of them helped her prepare a small exhibit for a local cultural festival, introducing her work to many first-time visitors. Nunes now hopes to convert part of her workshop into a demonstration space where tourists can watch tile painting and try the technique themselves.

【設問】
What helped Aveiro become known for producing azulejos?', NULL, '["Its clay-rich soil and canals for transporting finished tiles.","Its location near the capital city of Lisbon.","A law requiring all Portuguese buildings to use local tiles.","Its access to imported pigments from other countries."]', 0, '["第1段落：良質な粘土と運河による輸送の便がタイル産業を支えた。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題）', 906);
