Which of the following statements is true?', NULL, '["Ramesh Yadav established his workshop in 1901.","The number of hand-weaving workshops in Bhadohi has increased since 1996.","Yadav’s designs relied only on simple repeating geometric patterns.","Tiwari began weaving before her mother taught her the craft."]', 0, '["第3段落：Yadavは1901年に工房を設立と明記。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題）', 908);
INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('tgweb_english', '長文問題', 'プエブラの陶器（タラベラ）', 'Puebla, a city in central Mexico, has been known for a distinctive style of hand-painted pottery called talavera since the 16th century, when Spanish colonists introduced European ceramic techniques that blended with local indigenous traditions. The city’s access to fine clay deposits, along with strict guild regulations that controlled quality, helped talavera pottery earn a lasting reputation. In 2019, the traditional production process was recognized as part of Mexico’s Intangible Cultural Heritage.

Sofía Ramírez owns a small talavera workshop in Puebla’s historic center. She shapes each piece on a foot-powered wheel and paints intricate patterns using pigments made from natural minerals, following methods passed down within her family. Ramírez began her training in 2001, when Puebla had around 35 certified talavera workshops. Today, only 15 hold the certification required to use the traditional talavera name, as strict quality standards have caused some workshops to lose their status.

Ramírez often speaks of Ignacio Herrera, a potter who opened a workshop in Puebla in 1889. At the time, most talavera pieces used a narrow range of blue and white designs influenced heavily by imported Chinese porcelain. Herrera began incorporating yellow, green, and orange pigments alongside traditional blue, along with designs inspired by local flowers and birds. His innovations expanded the artistic range of talavera pottery while still respecting its established techniques.

A small bowl painted by Herrera is displayed prominently in Ramírez’s workshop. Like Herrera, she believes that tradition and creativity can coexist within the same craft. Ramírez has trained a number of apprentices over the years, and in 2022, one of them helped her organize a booth at an international craft fair, introducing her pottery to buyers from several countries. Ramírez now hopes to open a small gallery attached to her workshop, where visitors can view historic talavera pieces alongside her own work.

【設問】
How did talavera pottery originate in Puebla?', NULL, '["Spanish techniques blended with local indigenous pottery traditions.","It was invented entirely by indigenous artisans without outside influence.","It was imported directly from China and copied exactly.","It developed after Puebla’s clay deposits were discovered in the 20th century."]', 0, '["第1段落：スペインの技法と現地の伝統が融合して生まれた。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（TG-WEB新型英語: 長文問題）', 909);
